  "verseCount": 16,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "1",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "TIT 1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "1",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "po"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Paul, a servant of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ to further the faith of God's elect and their knowledge of the truth that leads to godliness—",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in the hope of eternal life, which God, who does not lie, promised before the beginning of time,",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and which now at his appointed season he has brought to light through the preaching entrusted to me by the command of God our Savior,",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "po"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To Titus, my true son in our common faith:",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "po",
        "vid": "TIT 1:4"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Savior.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Appointing Elders Who Love What Is Good",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The reason I left you in Crete was that you might put in order what was left unfinished and appoint",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "elders in every town, as I directed you.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An elder must be blameless, faithful to his wife, a man whose children believe",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "and are not open to the charge of being wild and disobedient.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Since an overseer manages God's household, he must be blameless—not overbearing, not quick-tempered, not given to drunkenness, not violent, not pursuing dishonest gain.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather, he must be hospitable, one who loves what is good, who is self-controlled, upright, holy and disciplined.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He must hold firmly to the trustworthy message as it has been taught, so that he can encourage others by sound doctrine and refute those who oppose it.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Rebuking Those Who Fail to Do Good",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For there are many rebellious people, full of meaningless talk and deception, especially those of the circumcision group.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They must be silenced, because they are disrupting whole households by teaching things they ought not to teach—and that for the sake of dishonest gain.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One of Crete's own prophets has said it: \"Cretans are always liars, evil brutes, lazy gluttons.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This saying is true. Therefore rebuke them sharply, so that they will be sound in the faith",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and will pay no attention to Jewish myths or to the merely human commands of those who reject the truth.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To the pure, all things are pure, but to those who are corrupted and do not believe, nothing is pure. In fact, both their minds and consciences are corrupted.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They claim to know God, but by their actions they deny him. They are detestable, disobedient and unfit for doing anything good.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "TIT.2",
    "number": "2",
    "bookId": "TIT"
  },
